---
description: Document build conventions for client facing docx deliverables
globs: build/docs/**,docs/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Markdown in docs/ is canonical. The docx is generated output and lives in out/.
Never edit a file in out/ directly. Edits go into the build script.

Before rebuilding a document the user has edited, diff against their version
and treat their file as authoritative.

# Format

- Arial throughout. US Letter, one inch margins.
- Title 24pt bold. Subtitle 18pt.
- Meta line 10pt grey: Confidential, month and year, Working File For Discussion.
- Section headings 16pt bold. Subsections 12pt bold.
- One line grey summaries at 11pt under headings.
- Body and bullets 11pt.
- No italics. No horizontal lines.
- Partnership document naming is Company plus Company.
